{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/153868-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-pack-creation","id":153868,"title":"Idigam Chronicles Weekly Discussion: Pack creation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-30T08:51:15-07:00","id":153868,"title":"Idigam Chronicles Weekly Discussion: Pack creation","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-gangs-all-here/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-gangs-all-here/\" target=\"_blank\"> The Gang&rsquo;s All Here &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-gangs-all-here/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/the-gangs-all-here/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well...it seems much like the 12 Steps of Blood &amp; Smoke, which I kinda like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T09:04:18-07:00","id":153909,"title":"","content":"I like this! Mostly because my players have a nasty tendency to pretty much ignore each other's character when making them. This will tie them a bit tighter together!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T09:51:44-07:00","id":153953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/153868-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-pack-creation?p=153909#post153909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this! Mostly because my players have a nasty tendency to pretty much ignore each other's character when making them. This will tie them a bit tighter together!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it says that everybody makes their characters first, which doesn't imply that this system forces them to make characters together.<br /> <br /> That having been said, I'm a fan of structured game/group generation, so this whole process is right up my alley. So far, except for the Idigam update, everything Stew's said about Werewolf has made me even more excited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T10:23:22-07:00","id":153967,"title":"","content":"Repost from the blog:<br /> <br /> As much as I was excited about having Wolf-Bloods and humans in a pack, I don't like how it is handled here. It makes the pack feel less like a close knit group and much more like the merit contacts added into the pack, like an organization or a cult. If the humans don't know anything about the werewolves and the totem, what separates them from normal retainers or other NPCs the werewolves have, aside from the totem bonuses? It also makes the werewolves in the group more the actual pack, with the rest just allies at best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T10:54:27-07:00","id":154011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/153868-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-pack-creation?p=153967#post153967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Repost from the blog: As much as I was excited about having Wolf-Bloods and humans in a pack, I don't like how it is handled here. It makes the pack feel less like a close knit group and much more like the merit contacts added into the pack, like an organization or a cult. If the humans don't know anything about the werewolves and the totem, what separates them from normal retainers or other NPCs the werewolves have, aside from the totem bonuses? It also makes the werewolves in the group more the actual pack, with the rest just allies at best.</div> </div> </div> </div> We've known that since the Packs spoiler all the way back on April 12th. The werewolves and the pack Totem form the core of the pack, the hunting party the performs the siskur-dah. Some packs allow wolf blooded into the hunting party, but it's rare because wolf blooded are not really equipped for the hunt, and it puts them at undue risk. Then the extended pack is made up of the wolf blooded members, and sometimes a few humans in-the-know. They are the lieutenants, who maintain the territory and deal with spirits and handle the pack's important duties while the hunting party is on the siskur-dah. Then there are the rest of the human members, who do not know, and generally think they're part of a biker gang, or a religious organization, or a secret society, or what ever. They join to be a part of something, they just don't know that something is a werewolf pack. They still benefit from the totem's protection as members of the pack, and they provide the in-the-know pack members with ties to normal life, as well as cover to blend in with among the flock.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T10:55:30-07:00","id":154014,"title":"","content":"Possible spirit packmates beyond the Totem? Aww yissssssssss!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T11:27:42-07:00","id":154041,"title":"","content":"I could see blood talons running with the lesser wolf spirits that accompany fenris-ur in the hisil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T12:42:45-07:00","id":154108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/153868-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-pack-creation?p=153967#post153967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Repost from the blog:<br /> <br /> As much as I was excited about having Wolf-Bloods and humans in a pack, I don't like how it is handled here. It makes the pack feel less like a close knit group and much more like the merit contacts added into the pack, like an organization or a cult. If the humans don't know anything about the werewolves and the totem, what separates them from normal retainers or other NPCs the werewolves have, aside from the totem bonuses? It also makes the werewolves in the group more the actual pack, with the rest just allies at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly forces your hand to play every pack with a secondary cast of Wolfblooded and/or normal humans? <b>The Herd Must Not Know</b><br /> <br /> Another pack keeps itself grounded around itself, Uratha only. Add humans or Blooded and it's more links to pick at to see which part of the chain gets loose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T13:10:09-07:00","id":154130,"title":"","content":"I dunno how their harmony might work with that, unless they're incredibly comfortable with themselves and not like to slip","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T13:19:54-07:00","id":154136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/153868-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-pack-creation?p=154108#post154108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What exactly forces your hand to play every pack with a secondary cast of Wolfblooded and/or normal humans? <b>The Herd Must Not Know</b><br /> <br /> Another pack keeps itself grounded around itself, Uratha only. Add humans or Blooded and it's more links to pick at to see which part of the chain gets loose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, I'm pretty certain the blog post about the pack said that 'Herd must not Know' doesn't apply to these humans in a pack.<br /> <br /> As for what forces my hand? Nothing, I just like the idea that packs can be varied mix between mostly human, mostly WBs to mostly uratha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T13:29:06-07:00","id":154141,"title":"","content":"The guy stated it was optional. If you want to make fully fleshed out wolf blooded and humans, that's something you can do as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T14:34:21-07:00","id":154181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/153868-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-pack-creation?p=154011#post154011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> We've known that since the Packs spoiler all the way back on April 12th. The werewolves and the pack Totem form the core of the pack, the hunting party the performs the siskur-dah. Some packs allow wolf blooded into the hunting party, but it's rare because wolf blooded are not really equipped for the hunt, and it puts them at undue risk. Then the extended pack is made up of the wolf blooded members, and sometimes a few humans in-the-know. They are the lieutenants, who maintain the territory and deal with spirits and handle the pack's important duties while the hunting party is on the siskur-dah. Then there are the rest of the human members, who do not know, and generally think they're part of a biker gang, or a religious organization, or a secret society, or what ever. They join to be a part of something, they just don't know that something is a werewolf pack. They still benefit from the totem's protection as members of the pack, and they provide the in-the-know pack members with ties to normal life, as well as cover to blend in with among the flock.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I guess I missed it ^^''<br /> <br /> I like the true companions feeling of packs, and this feels much more like an organization. But then, we haven't yet looked at the actual book, so I'm refraining from complaining from this now until I know more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T16:21:28-07:00","id":154253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/153868-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-pack-creation?p=154181#post154181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah, I guess I missed it ^^'' I like the true companions feeling of packs, and this feels much more like an organization. But then, we haven't yet looked at the actual book, so I'm refraining from complaining from this now until I know more.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think you'll still very much get that feel from the hunting party, and to a lesser extent the wolf blooded packmates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T16:49:34-07:00","id":154296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/153868-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-pack-creation?p=154014#post154014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possible spirit packmates beyond the Totem? Aww yissssssssss!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I feel about wolf packmates XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T19:27:57-07:00","id":154452,"title":"","content":"This is actually pretty awesome. It goes along with the nwod concept of giving the players more power. First with beats and now with this system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T11:35:15-07:00","id":155030,"title":"","content":"I find it intriguing the fact that apparently they're gonna devote more word-count to normal wolves within packs than the possibility of spirits as a full-blown packmate, for a number of reasons: First, there aren't wolves in every territory; Second, wolves don't strike me as nearly as much compelling a packmate as a person or a spirit would be. So if I was in the editor's shoes, I'd leave the sidebar to wolves or other canines as packmates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T11:51:50-07:00","id":155054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/153868-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-pack-creation?p=155030#post155030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it intriguing the fact that apparently they're gonna devote more word-count to normal wolves within packs than the possibility of spirits as a full-blown packmate, for a number of reasons: First, there aren't wolves in every territory; Second, wolves don't strike me as nearly as much compelling a packmate as a person or a spirit would be. So if I was in the editor's shoes, I'd leave the sidebar to wolves or other canines as packmates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn, missed that part in the blog. Still,cool!<br /> <br /> I think wolves need the extra space -because- they are not so commonly thought about as packmates. Spirits are easier to understand in a pack.<br /> <br /> Man, packs'll be one huge potpurri of creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T11:59:17-07:00","id":155083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/153868-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-pack-creation?p=155030#post155030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it intriguing the fact that apparently they're gonna devote more word-count to normal wolves within packs than the possibility of spirits as a full-blown packmate, for a number of reasons: First, there aren't wolves in every territory; Second, wolves don't strike me as nearly as much compelling a packmate as a person or a spirit would be. So if I was in the editor's shoes, I'd leave the sidebar to wolves or other canines as packmates.</div> </div> </div> </div> They're not. Both will only get a sidebar. To quote the blog, &quot;Unfortunately, we don't have the room to cover spirits and wolves as pack mates outside of a sidebar in the Idigam Chronicle itself; we're focusing on humans and Wolf-Blooded as the most likely to be protagonists or supporting characters.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T13:03:33-07:00","id":155119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/153868-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-pack-creation?p=155083#post155083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They're not. Both will only get a sidebar. To quote the blog, &quot;Unfortunately, we don't have the room to cover spirits and wolves as pack mates outside of a sidebar in the Idigam Chronicle itself; we're focusing on humans and Wolf-Blooded as the most likely to be protagonists or supporting characters.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the clarification there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T13:06:12-07:00","id":155121,"title":"","content":"With wolves as packmembers I wonder if we could see a return of Lupus-like characters from <b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</b>? Not on scale of &quot;werewolves very often comes from wolves families&quot;, but like character that come from time to time. I understand human-centrism of nWoD in general, but &quot;wolf-to-humans&quot; werewolves are large part of lore and one or two characters in chronicle would nicely broke the mold. With wolves as packmembers, wolf-born werewolves are almost must be it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T13:27:20-07:00","id":155158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/153868-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-pack-creation?p=155121#post155121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With wolves as packmembers I wonder if we could see a return of Lupus-like characters from <b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</b>? Not on scale of &amp;quot;werewolves very often comes from wolves families&amp;quot;, but like character that come from time to time. I understand human-centrism of nWoD in general, but &amp;quot;wolf-to-humans&amp;quot; werewolves are large part of lore and one or two characters in chronicle would nicely broke the mold. With wolves as packmembers, wolf-born werewolves are almost must be it.</div> </div> </div> </div> I've always loved the idea of born-from-wolf werewolves, but honestly, I'm glad they're not in Forsaken. The Uratha's connection to wolves is spiritual, not biological. [rant] Plus, Lupus are one of those character types that's too easy to play as an obnoxious stereotype. Just like Fishmalks in Masquerade and Kender in Dragonlance. Oh, you're an attractive female Lupus who never quite got the hang of certain human social conventions like the need to wear clothes? How original. [/rant]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T16:49:21-07:00","id":155304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/153868-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-pack-creation?p=155121#post155121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With wolves as packmembers I wonder if we could see a return of Lupus-like characters from <b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope not. Thematically, (IMO) they're a poor fit for Forsaken, but if you want to add them into your game as a house rule, there's nothing stopping it.<br /> <br /> What I'd like to see (half-formed idea alert) is a type of broken Wolf Spirit (or Wolf Host), that started by possessing and claiming wolves but then discovered that Mother Luna's and Father Wolf's tinkering to make Uratha had opened the door to make humans a 'natural' possession target for it/them. Over time, it forces its wolf hosts to become more human and its human hosts to be more feral, wolf-like and savage, thereby confusing the hell out of Uratha who don't know if this pack is a strange type of Wolf-Blooded, an Uratha gone wrong, an Idigam (if they know about them at all), or something completely new.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T17:31:55-07:00","id":155320,"title":"","content":"There is one canon werewolf born from wolf and werewolf. I think the idea of it being more commonplace doesn't fit as well in the nWoD, but that's just my opinion of the more low-key approach to the game. It has plenty of crazy things happening, but at first glance, the world works exactly how it does in real life.<br /> I think like many things, it's fine if you want it for your own game, but spending time/room explaining it in the core is unnecessary. Particularly since there'd be no mechanical difference, just a difference in the ways the players act.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-31-2014, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T17:36:42-07:00","id":155321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/153868-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-pack-creation?p=155320#post155320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is one canon werewolf born from wolf and werewolf. I think the idea of it being more commonplace doesn't fit as well in the nWoD, but that's just my opinion of the more low-key approach to the game. It has plenty of crazy things happening, but at first glance, the world works exactly how it does in real life.<br /> I think like many things, it's fine if you want it for your own game, but spending time/room explaining it in the core is unnecessary. Particularly since there'd be no mechanical difference, just a difference in the ways the players act.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and even that isn't completely certain. It could just as well be a propaganda piece for the Pure to boost morale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T17:48:37-07:00","id":155323,"title":"","content":"But it's the spirits that say his father was a Hunter in Darkness.<br /> <br /> Either way, the option is viable for groups who want it, and dismissed for groups who don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-31-2014, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T18:14:53-07:00","id":155334,"title":"","content":"It's funny, as much as I like the idea of the wolf-born and werewolf-born ...werewolves, the only idea I've had for a wolf-born one was a wolf that had been raised as a pet.<br /> <br /> Guess Toboe really was my favorite from that bunch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T19:57:11-07:00","id":155384,"title":"","content":"So I was expecting to see stuff about Totems in this spoiler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T20:33:59-07:00","id":155408,"title":"","content":"There is more then one wolf born werewolf, unless the hunter in darkness mentioned in (I think it's) tribes is the same as the father of the one in night horrors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T22:30:17-07:00","id":155460,"title":"","content":"I thought the Pure were born from wolves? Or is that just 'what they say'?<br /> <br /> Personally, I like the idea of a werewolf who's wolf-born although I can agree with some of the aforementioned concerns","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T22:46:28-07:00","id":155474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/153868-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-pack-creation?p=155460#post155460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the Pure were born from wolves? Or is that just 'what they say'?</div> </div> </div> </div>If that were even &quot;what they say&quot; then the Fire-Touched being the most infamous recruiters from the Forsaken would be even more shitcakes bananas than could be believably attributed to a self-professedly feverish hate-doctrine.<br /> <br /> The Pure draw more of their cultural viewpoint from &quot;might makes right and the Shadow is mighty&quot; and &quot;humans are weak and we are definitely not human&quot; than any claims of literal wolf-bloodedness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T22:48:20-07:00","id":155475,"title":"","content":"They'd love to be, they think it's pretty Pure, and the guy who was born from a wolf is considered a messiah among them. And certainly he seems to be good at what he does.<br /> <br /> But he does have some pretty major flaws, particularly in that he -may- be sterile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T22:51:39-07:00","id":155477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/153868-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-pack-creation?p=155474#post155474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that were even &quot;what they say&quot; then the Fire-Touched being the most infamous recruiters from the Forsaken would be even more shitcakes bananas than could be believably attributed to a self-professedly feverish hate-doctrine.<br /> <br /> The Pure draw more of their cultural viewpoint from &quot;might makes right and the Shadow is mighty&quot; and &quot;humans are weak and we are definitely not human&quot; than any claims of literal wolf-bloodedness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This Pure refernace connected with reproduction from wolves come to me recalling this scene...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://youtu.be/-loi7v7UEt8?t=1m7s\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;You wouldn't understand it...&quot;</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-01-2014, 01:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":